Stage 13's mkustar for rung gcc4 (19-gcc464 README, rung gcc4): libstdc++'s
headers put names of 100 bytes and more into /usr
(usr/include/c++/4.6.4/ext/pb_ds/detail/cc_hash_table_map_/...), and 40
more directories to rootfs-gcc3.tar's 36 (the table had 64). The first
gcc4 run stopped at packing with
`mkustar: name too long usr/include/c++/4.6.4/ext/pb_ds/...`. A long name
goes into the ustar prefix and name fields (rung-init reads the prefix);
the directory table holds 1024 names of up to 255 bytes. An archive whose
names are all under 99 bytes comes out byte for byte as before.

--- a/mkustar.c
+++ b/mkustar.c
@@ -3,8 +3,9 @@
